# What release/vttest.sh types into vttest 2.7 (20251205) at 24x80.80: a walk
# through every menu holding one of vttest's self-checks (the 48 source lines
# that print SHOW_SUCCESS or SHOW_FAILURE), each test reached once. One
# input per line: a menu choice, `*` (every choice of that menu), or `-`
# (Return, to a "Push <RETURN>"). A line `@3 KEY` is typed only when the
# terminal's operating level (from its DA) is 3 or more, `@<3 KEY` only
# below: vttest shows another menu, or none, by level there. Text after `#`
# is a comment. vttest.py turns this into vttest's own command file (-c).
#
# Left out, and why (vttest-expected.txt counts them as not reached):
# - DECBKM (11.3.4), the keyboard menus (5, 11.x keyboard-control) and the
#   mouse and locator reports: they read a key or click typed by a person.
# - VT52 (7) at level 3 or more: its DECSCL check waits for a Return typed
#   by a person when the terminal ignores DECRQSS in VT52 mode.
# - XTerm's DECRQSS menu (11.8.2.4): the same check line as VT320's, and a
#   number of holds that depends on the terminal's answers.

# 6: terminal reports
6
5      # DA2
-
6      # DA3
-
0
# 7: VT52 mode (at level 2 only, above)
@<3 7
@<3 -
@<3 -
@<3 -
